[04:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'also choose some examples in case you would like to test it first. You will notice that the prompt always starts with a person and then the animation comes. So, I can then choose here also another prompt. So, for example, a'

[05:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'person side steps to the right, and then I\'m going to hit update text prompt, and this is how you can then override the animation from what you had before. It will then load a little bit. Just give it some time, but then you will see that'

[05:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it already updates the animation quite well, and it\'s doing exactly what we want from the example itself. You can then also go to restart again, and this will then create a clean animation for you as well. So, when you play it now,'

[05:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you will see that it\'s much smoother already, and you can use it like this. But how can we now chain multiple animations together? What you have to do'

[05:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is that we\'re going back to text and then let\'s say at this point here we would like then to introduce a new animation. So, at the frame that we have right now here, I would then just give it a new prompt. So, I will input here'

[05:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something like a person runs forward, then stops and looks around alertly. We can then put this here by clicking at again update text prompt and you would then see that you have like two'

